OL,4,T]W-,,%-,,%-,,% ,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,5,B
OL,6, British troops with the peace-keeping
OL,7, force in Lebanon are to stay for the
OL,8, moment.
OL,9,B
OL,10,BThe armed forces minister, Mr John
OL,11,BStanley, returned from a visit to
OL,12,BBeirut and rejected any suggestion that
OL,13,Bthe troops were to be pulled out.
OL,14,B
OL,15,BLabour's foreign affairs spokesman Mr
OL,16,BDenis Healey suggested earlier this
OL,17,Bweek that the troops should be removed.
OL,18,B
OL,19,S/BIn an interview with US journalists
OL,20,BMrs Thatcher has defended the role of
OL,21,BBritish troops serving in Lebanon.
OL,22,B
OL,23,T]CFromG24-09-83C  teletextarchive.com
